   "text": {
    "L1": "India is linked to its neighbours by land, sea, rivers and culture.",
    "L2": "Pakistan, Afghanistan, China, Nepal, Bhutan, Bangladesh and Myanmar share land borders with India.",
    "L3": "Sri Lanka and the Maldives are sea neighbours. Sri Lanka lies across the narrow Palk Strait.",
    "L4": "The Himalayas run along India's northern border with Nepal, Bhutan and China.",
    "L5": "The Brahmaputra begins in Tibet as the Yarlung Tsangpo, enters India, flows through Assam, and continues into Bangladesh.",
    "L6": "A river does not stop at a national border. Upstream rain, dams or pollution can affect people downstream.",
    "L7": "Shared rivers, floods, trade, transport and culture give neighbours reasons to cooperate."
   },
